IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa18-part23-ch1.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 23 (distributions), Chapter 1 (restrictions on when
-- distributions may be made), ss 829 to 835. Lines 11119-11234 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- How to read an answer (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING) is as in the header of coa18-part22-notice.l4. Money is NUMBER
-- (pounds); a percentage is a fraction.
--
-- SEAMS (inputs, never imports): `s 4(2) the company is a public company` (BOOLEAN); `s 395 ...` (Companies Act accounts or
-- IAS accounts: the type `s 831(3) kind of relevant accounts` below, used by the whole of Part 23); `s 396 the provision is
-- of a kind specified ...` (MAYBE BOOLEAN); `s 1165(2) the company is an authorised insurance company` (BOOLEAN);
-- `Part 18 Chapter 3, 4 or 5 ...` (MAYBE BOOLEAN).
-- ANSWERS OTHER PARTS ASK FOR (PLAN section 6): `s 829(1) the act is a distribution`; `s 830(2) the profits available for
-- distribution` (NUMBER); `s 831(4) the company's undistributable reserves` (NUMBER); `s 833(1) the company is an
-- investment company`.

§ `Part 23 (ss 829 to 853), Chapter 1: ss 829 to 835`

-- The two kinds of accounts that Part 23 distinguishes throughout (the Act's own index sends "Companies Act accounts" and
-- "IAS accounts" to s 395, in coa8): declared once here, under the first section that uses the distinction.
DECLARE `s 831(3) kind of relevant accounts` IS ONE OF
    `s 831(3)(a) Companies Act accounts`
    `s 831(3)(b) IAS accounts`
    `s 831(3) accounts of another kind`

§§ `s 829 Meaning of "distribution"`

DECLARE `s 829(2) description of act` IS ONE OF
    `s 829(2)(a) an issue of shares as fully or partly paid bonus shares`
    `s 829(2)(b)(i) a reduction of share capital by extinguishing or reducing the liability of any of the members on any of the company's shares in respect of share capital not paid up`
    `s 829(2)(b)(ii) a reduction of share capital by repaying paid-up share capital`
    `s 829(2)(c) the redemption or purchase of any of the company's own shares out of capital (including the proceeds of any fresh issue of shares) or out of unrealised profits`
    `s 829(2)(d) a distribution of assets to members of the company on its winding up`
    `s 829(1) another description of distribution of the company's assets to its members, whether in cash or otherwise`
    `s 829(1) something that is not a distribution of the company's assets to its members`

-- src:11124 | (2) The following are not distributions for the purposes of this Part—
-- src:11125 | (a) an issue of shares as fully or partly paid bonus shares;
-- src:11126 | (b) the reduction of share capital—
-- src:11127 | (i) by extinguishing or reducing the liability of any of the members on any of the company's shares in respect of share capital not paid up, or
-- src:11128 | (ii) by repaying paid-up share capital;
-- src:11129 | (c) the redemption or purchase of any of the company's own shares out of capital (including the proceeds of any fresh issue of shares) or out of unrealised profits in accordance with Chapter 3, 4 or 5 of Part 18;
-- src:11130 | (d) a distribution of assets to members of the company on its winding up.
@ref s 829(2) Meaning of "distribution" (src:11124-11130)
GIVEN act IS A `s 829(2) description of act`
      `Part 18 Chapter 3, 4 or 5 the redemption or purchase of the shares out of capital or unrealised profits is in accordance with the Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 829(2) the act is not a distribution for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 829(2)(a) an issue of shares as fully or partly paid bonus shares` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 829(2)(b)(i) a reduction of share capital by extinguishing or reducing the liability of any of the members on any of the company's shares in respect of share capital not paid up` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 829(2)(b)(ii) a reduction of share capital by repaying paid-up share capital` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 829(2)(c) the redemption or purchase of any of the company's own shares out of capital (including the proceeds of any fresh issue of shares) or out of unrealised profits` THEN
        CONSIDER `Part 18 Chapter 3, 4 or 5 the redemption or purchase of the shares out of capital or unrealised profits is in accordance with the Chapter`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in accordance with Chapter 3, 4 or 5 of Part 18": whether the redemption or purchase is in accordance with those Chapters is answered in Part 18 (a redemption not in accordance falls outside the exception)
    WHEN `s 829(2)(d) a distribution of assets to members of the company on its winding up` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) lists the acts that are not distributions; it says nothing of an act it does not list

-- src:11122 | 829 Meaning of “distribution”
-- src:11123 | (1) In this Part “distribution” means every description of distribution of a company's assets to its members, whether in cash or otherwise, subject to the following exceptions.
@ref s 829(1) Meaning of "distribution" (src:11122-11123)
GIVEN act IS A `s 829(2) description of act`
      `Part 18 Chapter 3, 4 or 5 the redemption or purchase of the shares out of capital or unrealised profits is in accordance with the Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 829(1) the act is a distribution` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 829(1) something that is not a distribution of the company's assets to its members` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part “distribution” means every description of distribution of a company's assets to its members, whether in cash or otherwise"
    WHEN `s 829(1) another description of distribution of the company's assets to its members, whether in cash or otherwise` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `s 829(2) the act is not a distribution for the purposes of this Part` act `Part 18 Chapter 3, 4 or 5 the redemption or purchase of the shares out of capital or unrealised profits is in accordance with the Chapter`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following are not distributions for the purposes of this Part"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an act in the s 829(2)(c) description that is not shown to be in accordance with Part 18 Chapter 3, 4 or 5 is not decided by this section

§§ `s 830 Distributions to be made only out of profits available for the purpose`

-- (2): the profits available for distribution: accumulated, realised profits not previously utilised by distribution or
-- capitalisation, less accumulated, realised losses not previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital
-- duly made. A negative figure means there are no profits available.
-- src:11134 | (2) A company's profits available for distribution are its accumulated, realised profits, so far as not previously utilised by distribution or capitalisation, less its accumulated, realised losses, so far as not previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made.
@ref s 830(2) Distributions to be made only out of profits available for the purpose (src:11134-11134)
GIVEN `the company's accumulated, realised profits` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of those profits previously utilised by distribution or capitalisation` IS A NUMBER
      `the company's accumulated, realised losses` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of those losses previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 830(2) the profits available for distribution` MEANS
    (`the company's accumulated, realised profits` MINUS `the part of those profits previously utilised by distribution or capitalisation`)
    MINUS (`the company's accumulated, realised losses` MINUS `the part of those losses previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made`)

-- (1): "may only make a distribution out of profits available for the purpose": the distribution is within the limit, or it is not.
-- src:11133 | (1) A company may only make a distribution out of profits available for the purpose.
@ref s 830(1) Distributions to be made only out of profits available for the purpose (src:11133-11133)
GIVEN `the amount of the distribution` IS A NUMBER
      `the profits available for distribution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 830(1) the distribution is within the profits available for the purpose` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the distribution` AT MOST `the profits available for distribution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may only make a distribution out of profits available for the purpose."

-- src:11135 | (3) Subsection (2) has effect subject to sections 832 , 833A and 835 (investment companies and Solvency 2 insurance companies).
@ref s 830(3) Distributions to be made only out of profits available for the purpose (src:11135-11135)
GIVEN `section 832, 833A or 835 applies to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 830(3) subsection (2) has effect subject to sections 832, 833A and 835` MEANS
    IF `section 832, 833A or 835 applies to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (2) has effect subject to sections 832 , 833A and 835 (investment companies and Solvency 2 insurance companies)": a company outside those sections is not mentioned

§§ `s 831 Net asset restriction on distributions by public companies`

-- src:11136 | 831 Net asset restriction on distributions by public companies
-- src:11137 | (1) A public company may only make a distribution—
-- src:11138 | (a) if the amount of its net assets is not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves, and
-- src:11139 | (b) if, and to the extent that, the distribution does not reduce the amount of those assets to less than that aggregate.
@ref s 831(1) Net asset restriction on distributions by public companies (src:11136-11139)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the company's net assets` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the company's called-up share capital` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the company's undistributable reserves` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the distribution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 831(1) the distribution is within the net asset restriction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `s 4(2) the company is a public company`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company may only make a distribution": a private company is not mentioned (section 830 still applies to it)
        IF     `the amount of the company's net assets` AT LEAST (`the amount of the company's called-up share capital` PLUS `the amount of the company's undistributable reserves`)
           AND (`the amount of the company's net assets` MINUS `the amount of the distribution`) AT LEAST (`the amount of the company's called-up share capital` PLUS `the amount of the company's undistributable reserves`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A public company may only make a distribution— (a) if the amount of its net assets is not less than the aggregate of its called-up share capital and undistributable reserves, and (b) if, and to the extent that, the distribution does not reduce the amount of those assets to less than that aggregate."

-- src:11140 | (2) For this purpose a company's “net assets” means the aggregate of the company's assets less the aggregate of its liabilities.
@ref s 831(2) Net asset restriction on distributions by public companies (src:11140-11140)
GIVEN `the aggregate of the company's assets` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the company's liabilities` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 831(2) the company's net assets` MEANS
    `the aggregate of the company's assets` MINUS `the aggregate of the company's liabilities`

-- src:11141 | (3) “Liabilities” here includes—
-- src:11142 | (a) where the relevant accounts are Companies Act accounts, provisions of a kind specified for the purposes of this subsection by regulations under section 396;
-- src:11143 | (b) where the relevant accounts are IAS accounts, provisions of any kind.
@ref s 831(3) Net asset restriction on distributions by public companies (src:11141-11143)
GIVEN accounts IS A `s 831(3) kind of relevant accounts`
      `s 396 the provision is of a kind specified for the purposes of section 831(3) by regulations under section 396` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 831(3) the provision is included in liabilities` MEANS
    CONSIDER accounts
    WHEN `s 831(3)(a) Companies Act accounts` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 396 the provision is of a kind specified for the purposes of section 831(3) by regulations under section 396`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“Liabilities” here includes— (a) where the relevant accounts are Companies Act accounts, provisions of a kind specified for the purposes of this subsection by regulations under section 396": the kinds so specified are in s 396 (outside this Part); "includes" does not close the list
    WHEN `s 831(3)(b) IAS accounts` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“Liabilities” here includes ..." names Companies Act accounts and IAS accounts only

-- (4): the undistributable reserves: (a) share premium account; (b) capital redemption reserve; (c) the amount by which
-- accumulated, unrealised profits (so far as not previously utilised by capitalisation) exceed accumulated, unrealised losses
-- (so far as not previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made); (d) any other reserve the
-- company is prohibited from distributing by an enactment (other than one in this Part) or by its articles. Last sentence: a
-- transfer of profits to the capital redemption reserve is not "capitalisation" for (c).
-- src:11144 | (4) A company's undistributable reserves are—
-- src:11145 | (a) its share premium account;
-- src:11146 | (b) its capital redemption reserve;
-- src:11147 | (c) the amount by which its accumulated, unrealised profits (so far as not previously utilised by capitalisation) exceed its accumulated, unrealised losses (so far as not previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made);
-- src:11148 | (d) any other reserve that the company is prohibited from distributing—
-- src:11149 | (i) by any enactment (other than one contained in this Part), or
-- src:11150 | (ii) by its articles.
-- src:11151 | The reference in paragraph (c) to capitalisation does not include a transfer of profits of the company to its capital redemption reserve.
@ref s 831(4) Net asset restriction on distributions by public companies (src:11144-11151)
GIVEN `the amount of the company's share premium account` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the company's capital redemption reserve` IS A NUMBER
      `the company's accumulated, unrealised profits` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of those profits previously utilised by capitalisation, including transfers of profits to the capital redemption reserve` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of that utilisation that was a transfer of profits to the capital redemption reserve` IS A NUMBER
      `the company's accumulated, unrealised losses` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of those losses previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of any other reserve the company is prohibited from distributing by an enactment (other than one contained in this Part)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of any other reserve the company is prohibited from distributing by its articles` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 831(4) the company's undistributable reserves` MEANS
        `the amount of the company's share premium account`
    PLUS `the amount of the company's capital redemption reserve`
    PLUS (IF excess GREATER THAN 0 THEN excess ELSE 0)
    PLUS `the amount of any other reserve the company is prohibited from distributing by an enactment (other than one contained in this Part)`
    PLUS `the amount of any other reserve the company is prohibited from distributing by its articles`
    WHERE
        excess MEANS
            (`the company's accumulated, unrealised profits` MINUS (`the part of those profits previously utilised by capitalisation, including transfers of profits to the capital redemption reserve` MINUS `the part of that utilisation that was a transfer of profits to the capital redemption reserve`))
            MINUS (`the company's accumulated, unrealised losses` MINUS `the part of those losses previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made`)

-- src:11152 | (5) A public company must not include any uncalled share capital as an asset in any accounts relevant for purposes of this section.
@ref s 831(5) Net asset restriction on distributions by public companies (src:11152-11152)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 831(5) the company may include uncalled share capital as an asset in any accounts relevant for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A public company must not include any uncalled share capital as an asset in any accounts relevant for purposes of this section."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company must not include": a private company is not mentioned

-- src:11153 | (6) Subsection (1) has effect subject to sections 832 and 835 (investment companies etc: distributions out of accumulated revenue profits).
@ref s 831(6) Net asset restriction on distributions by public companies (src:11153-11153)
GIVEN `section 832 or 835 applies to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 831(6) subsection (1) has effect subject to sections 832 and 835` MEANS
    IF `section 832 or 835 applies to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) has effect subject to sections 832 and 835 (investment companies etc: distributions out of accumulated revenue profits)": a company outside those sections is not mentioned

§§ `s 832 Distributions by investment companies out of accumulated revenue profits`

-- (6)(b): the relevant period begins on the first day of the accounting reference period immediately preceding that in
-- which the distribution is to be made, or (if the distribution is in the company's first accounting reference period) on the
-- first day of that period, and ends with the date of the distribution. (6)(a) is shown as dots in the text.
-- src:11172 | (6) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:11173 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:11174 | (b) the “relevant period” is the period beginning with—
-- src:11175 | (i) the first day of the accounting reference period immediately preceding that in which the proposed distribution is to be made, or
-- src:11176 | (ii) where the distribution is to be made in the company's first accounting reference period, the first day of that period,
-- src:11177 | and ending with the date of the distribution.
@ref s 832(6) Distributions by investment companies out of accumulated revenue profits (src:11172-11177)
GIVEN `the distribution is to be made in the company's first accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the accounting reference period in which the distribution is to be made` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the accounting reference period immediately preceding that in which the distribution is to be made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 832(6)(b) the first day of the relevant period` MEANS
    IF `the distribution is to be made in the company's first accounting reference period`
    THEN `the first day of the accounting reference period in which the distribution is to be made`
    ELSE `the first day of the accounting reference period immediately preceding that in which the distribution is to be made`

-- src:11157 | (2) It may make such a distribution only if, and to the extent that, its accumulated, realised revenue profits, so far as not previously utilised by a distribution or capitalisation, exceed its accumulated revenue losses (whether realised or unrealised), so far as not previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made.
@ref s 832(2) Distributions by investment companies out of accumulated revenue profits (src:11157-11157)
GIVEN `the company's accumulated, realised revenue profits` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of those profits previously utilised by a distribution or capitalisation` IS A NUMBER
      `the company's accumulated revenue losses (whether realised or unrealised)` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of those losses previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the distribution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 832(2) the distribution is within the accumulated, realised revenue profits` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the distribution` AT MOST
         ((`the company's accumulated, realised revenue profits` MINUS `the part of those profits previously utilised by a distribution or capitalisation`)
          MINUS (`the company's accumulated revenue losses (whether realised or unrealised)` MINUS `the part of those losses previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It may make such a distribution only if, and to the extent that, its accumulated, realised revenue profits, so far as not previously utilised by a distribution or capitalisation, exceed its accumulated revenue losses (whether realised or unrealised), so far as not previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made."

-- src:11158 | (3) It may make such a distribution only—
-- src:11159 | (a) if the amount of its assets is at least equal to one and a half times the aggregate of its liabilities to creditors, and
-- src:11160 | (b) if, and to the extent that, the distribution does not reduce that amount to less than one and a half times that aggregate.
@ref s 832(3) Distributions by investment companies out of accumulated revenue profits (src:11158-11160)
GIVEN `the amount of the company's assets` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the company's liabilities to creditors` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the distribution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 832(3) the distribution is within the asset cover the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `the amount of the company's assets` AT LEAST (1.5 TIMES `the aggregate of the company's liabilities to creditors`)
       AND (`the amount of the company's assets` MINUS `the amount of the distribution`) AT LEAST (1.5 TIMES `the aggregate of the company's liabilities to creditors`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It may make such a distribution only— (a) if the amount of its assets is at least equal to one and a half times the aggregate of its liabilities to creditors, and (b) if, and to the extent that, the distribution does not reduce that amount to less than one and a half times that aggregate."

-- src:11161 | (4) For this purpose a company's liabilities to creditors include—
-- src:11162 | (a) in the case of Companies Act accounts, provisions of a kind specified for the purposes of this subsection by regulations under section 396;
-- src:11163 | (b) in the case of IAS accounts, provisions for liabilities to creditors.
@ref s 832(4) Distributions by investment companies out of accumulated revenue profits (src:11161-11163)
GIVEN accounts IS A `s 831(3) kind of relevant accounts`
      `s 396 the provision is of a kind specified for the purposes of section 832(4) by regulations under section 396` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the provision is a provision for liabilities to creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 832(4) the provision is included in the company's liabilities to creditors` MEANS
    CONSIDER accounts
    WHEN `s 831(3)(a) Companies Act accounts` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 396 the provision is of a kind specified for the purposes of section 832(4) by regulations under section 396`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a company's liabilities to creditors include— (a) in the case of Companies Act accounts, provisions of a kind specified ... by regulations under section 396": the kinds are in s 396 (outside this Part); "include" does not close the list
    WHEN `s 831(3)(b) IAS accounts` THEN
        IF `the provision is a provision for liabilities to creditors`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "(b) in the case of IAS accounts, provisions for liabilities to creditors": "include" does not close the list
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include" names Companies Act accounts and IAS accounts only

-- (5): the further conditions. (a) the company's shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market; (b) during the
-- relevant period it has not applied any unrealised profits in paying up debentures or amounts unpaid on its issued shares
-- ((b)(i) is shown as dots in the text); (c) it gave notice to the registrar under s 833(1) (i) before the relevant period
-- began, or (ii) as soon as reasonably practicable after incorporation.
-- src:11164 | (5) The following conditions must also be met—
-- src:11165 | (a) the company's shares must be shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market;
-- src:11166 | (b) during the relevant period it must not have—
-- src:11167 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:11168 | (ii) applied any unrealised profits . . . in paying up debentures or amounts unpaid on its issued shares;
-- src:11169 | (c) it must have given notice to the registrar under section 833(1) (notice of intention to carry on business as an investment company)—
-- src:11170 | (i) before the beginning of the relevant period, or
-- src:11171 | (ii) as soon as reasonably practicable after the date of its incorporation.
@ref s 832(5) Distributions by investment companies out of accumulated revenue profits (src:11164-11171)
GIVEN `the company's shares are shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `during the relevant period the company has applied unrealised profits in paying up debentures or amounts unpaid on its issued shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the company gave notice to the registrar under section 833(1)` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the relevant period` IS A DATE
      `the notice was given as soon as reasonably practicable after the date of the company's incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 832(5) the further conditions are met` MEANS
    IF     `the company's shares are shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
       AND (NOT `during the relevant period the company has applied unrealised profits in paying up debentures or amounts unpaid on its issued shares`)
       AND (   Day `the date on which the company gave notice to the registrar under section 833(1)` LESS THAN Day `the first day of the relevant period`
            OR `the notice was given as soon as reasonably practicable after the date of the company's incorporation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following conditions must also be met— (a) the company's shares must be shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market; (b) during the relevant period it must not have— ... (ii) applied any unrealised profits ... in paying up debentures or amounts unpaid on its issued shares; (c) it must have given notice to the registrar under section 833(1) ... (i) before the beginning of the relevant period, or (ii) as soon as reasonably practicable after the date of its incorporation."

-- src:11178 | (7) The company must not include any uncalled share capital as an asset in any accounts relevant for purposes of this section.
@ref s 832(7) Distributions by investment companies out of accumulated revenue profits (src:11178-11178)
GIVEN `the accounts include uncalled share capital as an asset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 832(7) the company may include uncalled share capital as an asset in any accounts relevant for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the accounts include uncalled share capital as an asset`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must not include any uncalled share capital as an asset in any accounts relevant for purposes of this section."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection forbids including uncalled share capital as an asset and says nothing of accounts that do not

-- (1): the grant: an investment company may make a distribution out of its accumulated, realised revenue profits if the
-- conditions are met: the answers of subsections (2), (3), (5) and (7) are passed in as MAYBE BOOLEANs by the caller.
-- src:11156 | (1) An investment company may make a distribution out of its accumulated, realised revenue profits if the following conditions are met.
@ref s 832(1) Distributions by investment companies out of accumulated revenue profits (src:11156-11156)
GIVEN `the company is an investment company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 832(2) the distribution is within the accumulated, realised revenue profits` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 832(3) the distribution is within the asset cover the subsection requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 832(5) the further conditions are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 832(7) the company may include uncalled share capital as an asset in any accounts relevant for the purposes of this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 832(1) the investment company may make the distribution out of its accumulated, realised revenue profits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the company is an investment company`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An investment company may make a distribution": another company is not mentioned
        IF `s 832(2) the distribution is within the accumulated, realised revenue profits` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 832(3) the distribution is within the asset cover the subsection requires` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 832(5) the further conditions are met` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 832(7) the company may include uncalled share capital as an asset in any accounts relevant for the purposes of this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An investment company may make a distribution out of its accumulated, realised revenue profits if the following conditions are met."
        IF `s 832(2) the distribution is within the accumulated, realised revenue profits` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 832(3) the distribution is within the asset cover the subsection requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 832(5) the further conditions are met` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known

§§ `s 833 Meaning of "investment company"`

-- src:11183 | (2) The requirement is—
-- src:11184 | (a) that the business of the company consists of investing its funds in shares, land or other assets, with the aim of spreading investment risk and giving members of the company the benefit of the results of the management of its funds;
-- src:11185 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:11186 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:11187 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:11188 | (3) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 833(2) Meaning of "investment company" (src:11183-11188)
GIVEN `the business of the company consists of investing its funds in shares, land or other assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aim is spreading investment risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aim is giving members of the company the benefit of the results of the management of its funds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833(2)(a) the requirement is met` MEANS
    IF     `the business of the company consists of investing its funds in shares, land or other assets`
       AND `the aim is spreading investment risk`
       AND `the aim is giving members of the company the benefit of the results of the management of its funds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirement is— (a) that the business of the company consists of investing its funds in shares, land or other assets, with the aim of spreading investment risk and giving members of the company the benefit of the results of the management of its funds" (paragraphs (b) to (d) are shown as dots in the text)

-- src:11179 | 833 Meaning of “investment company”
-- src:11180 | (1) In this Part an “investment company” means a public company that—
-- src:11181 | (a) has given notice (which has not been revoked) to the registrar of its intention to carry on business as an investment company, and
-- src:11182 | (b) since the date of that notice has complied with the following requirement.
@ref s 833(1) Meaning of "investment company" (src:11179-11182)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has given notice to the registrar of its intention to carry on business as an investment company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that notice has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `since the date of that notice the company has complied with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833(1) the company is an investment company` MEANS
    IF     `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
       AND `the company has given notice to the registrar of its intention to carry on business as an investment company`
       AND (NOT `that notice has been revoked`)
       AND `since the date of that notice the company has complied with the requirement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part an “investment company” means a public company that— (a) has given notice (which has not been revoked) to the registrar of its intention to carry on business as an investment company, and (b) since the date of that notice has complied with the following requirement."

-- (3) is shown as dots in the text.
-- src:11189 | (4) Notice to the registrar under this section may be revoked at any time by the company on giving notice to the registrar that it no longer wishes to be an investment company within the meaning of this section.
-- src:11190 | (5) On giving such a notice, the company ceases to be such a company.
@ref s 833(4) Meaning of "investment company" (src:11189-11190)
GIVEN `the company gives notice to the registrar that it no longer wishes to be an investment company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833(4) the notice to the registrar of intention to carry on business as an investment company is revoked` MEANS
    IF `the company gives notice to the registrar that it no longer wishes to be an investment company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Notice to the registrar under this section may be revoked at any time by the company on giving notice to the registrar that it no longer wishes to be an investment company": revocation another way is not mentioned

@ref s 833(5) Meaning of "investment company" (src:11190-11190)
GIVEN `the company gives notice under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833(5) the company ceases to be an investment company` MEANS
    IF `the company gives notice under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On giving such a notice, the company ceases to be such a company.": ceasing another way (for example by not complying with the requirement) is s 833(1)

§§ `s 833A Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive`

-- src:11191 | 833A Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive
-- src:11192 | (1) This section applies in relation to any authorised insurance company carrying on long-term business that is authorised in accordance with Article 14 of the Solvency 2 Directive.
@ref s 833A(1) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11191-11192)
GIVEN `s 1165(2) the company is an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company carries on long-term business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is authorised in accordance with Article 14 of the Solvency 2 Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833A(1) this section applies in relation to the company` MEANS
    IF     `s 1165(2) the company is an authorised insurance company`
       AND `the company carries on long-term business`
       AND `the company is authorised in accordance with Article 14 of the Solvency 2 Directive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies in relation to any authorised insurance company carrying on long-term business that is authorised in accordance with Article 14 of the Solvency 2 Directive."

-- (5): the items within the subsection, whose total is "D" in the formula in (4). Each paragraph's amount is a plain input;
-- an excess counts only if it is positive; (6) counts anything within more than one paragraph once (the caller passes the
-- amount counted twice).
-- src:11201 | (5) The items within this subsection are—
-- src:11202 | (a) if the value of shares held by the company in a qualifying investment subsidiary exceeds the value of the consideration given by it for their acquisition, the amount of that excess;
-- src:11203 | (b) any asset of the company representing a surplus in a defined benefit pension scheme;
-- src:11204 | (c) if the value of the assets held by the company in a ring-fenced fund exceeds the value of the liabilities incurred by the company in respect of that fund, the amount of that excess;
-- src:11205 | (d) the amount of any liability of the company in respect of deferred tax shown in the company’s balance sheet that relates to any asset within paragraph (a), (b) or (c);
-- src:11206 | (e) if—
-- src:11207 | (i) the company has permission to disapply or modify its rules in accordance with section 138BA of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, such that the company may apply a matching adjustment to a relevant risk-free interest rate term structure to calculate the best estimate of a portfolio of the company’s life insurance or reinsurance obligations, and
-- src:11208 | (ii) the value of the portfolio of the company’s assets assigned by the company to cover the best estimate exceeds the value of the portfolio of the company’s life insurance or reinsurance obligations,
-- src:11209 | the amount of that excess; and
-- src:11210 | (f) the following capital items of the company—
-- src:11211 | (i) paid-in ordinary share capital together with any related share premium account;
-- src:11212 | (ii) paid-in preference shares which are not liabilities of the company together with any related share premium account;
-- src:11213 | (iii) capital redemption reserve; and
-- src:11214 | (iv) any other reserve that the company is prohibited from distributing (ignoring this Part for this purpose).
-- src:11215 | (6) So far as anything falls within more than one of the above paragraphs of subsection (5), its value is to be taken into account only once.
@ref s 833A(5) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11201-11215)
GIVEN `the value of shares held by the company in a qualifying investment subsidiary` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the consideration given by it for their acquisition` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of any asset of the company representing a surplus in a defined benefit pension scheme` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the assets held by the company in a ring-fenced fund` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the liabilities incurred by the company in respect of that fund` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of any liability of the company in respect of deferred tax shown in the company's balance sheet that relates to any asset within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A NUMBER
      `the company has permission to disapply or modify its rules in accordance with section 138BA of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 such that it may apply a matching adjustment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the portfolio of the company's assets assigned to cover the best estimate` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the portfolio of the company's life insurance or reinsurance obligations` IS A NUMBER
      `the paid-in ordinary share capital together with any related share premium account` IS A NUMBER
      `the paid-in preference shares which are not liabilities of the company together with any related share premium account` IS A NUMBER
      `the capital redemption reserve` IS A NUMBER
      `any other reserve that the company is prohibited from distributing (ignoring this Part for this purpose)` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of anything taken into account under more than one of the paragraphs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 833A(5) the total value of the items within the subsection` MEANS
        excess `the value of shares held by the company in a qualifying investment subsidiary` `the value of the consideration given by it for their acquisition`
    PLUS `the value of any asset of the company representing a surplus in a defined benefit pension scheme`
    PLUS excess `the value of the assets held by the company in a ring-fenced fund` `the value of the liabilities incurred by the company in respect of that fund`
    PLUS `the amount of any liability of the company in respect of deferred tax shown in the company's balance sheet that relates to any asset within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`
    PLUS (IF `the company has permission to disapply or modify its rules in accordance with section 138BA of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 such that it may apply a matching adjustment` THEN excess `the value of the portfolio of the company's assets assigned to cover the best estimate` `the value of the portfolio of the company's life insurance or reinsurance obligations` ELSE 0)
    PLUS (   `the paid-in ordinary share capital together with any related share premium account`
          PLUS `the paid-in preference shares which are not liabilities of the company together with any related share premium account`
          PLUS `the capital redemption reserve`
          PLUS `any other reserve that the company is prohibited from distributing (ignoring this Part for this purpose)`)
    MINUS `the value of anything taken into account under more than one of the paragraphs`
    WHERE
        GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        excess MEANS IF a GREATER THAN b THEN a MINUS b ELSE 0

-- src:11195 | (4) The formula is A − L − D ,
-- src:11196 | where—
-- src:11197 | “A” is the total value of the company’s assets;
-- src:11198 | “L” is the total value of the company’s liabilities; and
-- src:11199 | “D” is the total value of the items within subsection (5) relating to the company;
-- src:11200 | and, in each case, the value is to be determined as at the date of the company’s balance sheet that forms part of the accounts mentioned in subsection (2).
@ref s 833A(4) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11195-11200)
GIVEN `the total value of the company's assets` IS A NUMBER
      `the total value of the company's liabilities` IS A NUMBER
      `the total value of the items within subsection (5) relating to the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 833A(4) the amount given by the formula A - L - D` MEANS
    `the total value of the company's assets` MINUS `the total value of the company's liabilities` MINUS `the total value of the items within subsection (5) relating to the company`

-- (2): the amount given by the formula is the realised profit (if positive) or the realised loss (if negative) of the company
-- for the period of the relevant accounts, for the purposes of s 830(2).
-- src:11193 | (2) For the purposes of section 830(2), the realised profit or loss of the company for the period in respect of which its relevant accounts (within the meaning of section 836) are prepared is taken to be the amount given by the formula in subsection (4) (with a positive figure taken to be a realised profit and a negative figure taken to be a realised loss).
@ref s 833A(2) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11193-11193)
GIVEN `the amount given by the formula in subsection (4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833A(2) the amount is taken to be a realised profit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount given by the formula in subsection (4)` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the amount given by the formula in subsection (4)` LESS THAN 0 THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with a positive figure taken to be a realised profit and a negative figure taken to be a realised loss": a negative figure is a realised loss
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a figure of nil is neither a profit nor a loss

@ref s 833A(2) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11193-11193)
GIVEN `the amount given by the formula in subsection (4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 833A(2) the realised profit (positive) or realised loss (negative) of the company for the period of its relevant accounts` MEANS
    `the amount given by the formula in subsection (4)`

-- src:11194 | (3) But the company’s profits available for distribution are limited to an amount that does not exceed its accumulated profits (whether realised or not), so far as not previously utilised by distribution or capitalisation, less its accumulated losses (whether realised or not), so far as not previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made.
@ref s 833A(3) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11194-11194)
GIVEN `the profits available for distribution under section 830(2) as it applies by virtue of subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the company's accumulated profits (whether realised or not)` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of those profits previously utilised by distribution or capitalisation` IS A NUMBER
      `the company's accumulated losses (whether realised or not)` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of those losses previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 833A(3) the company's profits available for distribution as limited by the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the profits available for distribution under section 830(2) as it applies by virtue of subsection (2)` AT MOST ceiling
    THEN `the profits available for distribution under section 830(2) as it applies by virtue of subsection (2)`
    ELSE ceiling
    WHERE
        ceiling MEANS
            (`the company's accumulated profits (whether realised or not)` MINUS `the part of those profits previously utilised by distribution or capitalisation`)
            MINUS (`the company's accumulated losses (whether realised or not)` MINUS `the part of those losses previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital duly made`)

-- src:11216 | (7) The company’s assets and liabilities must be valued in accordance with—
-- src:11217 | (a) Part 2 of the Insurance and Reinsurance Undertakings (Prudential Requirements) Regulations 2023 (prudential requirements),
-- src:11218 | (b) rules made by the Prudential Regulation Authority under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 in relation to the matching adjustment referred to in subsection (5)(e)(i),
-- src:11219 | (c) other rules made by the Authority under that Part implementing Articles 75 to 85 and 308b to 308e of the Solvency 2 Directive, and
-- src:11220 | (d) Articles 7 to 52 and 55 to 61 of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2015/35 supplementing that Directive.
@ref s 833A(7) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11216-11220)
GIVEN `the assets and liabilities are valued in accordance with Part 2 of the Insurance and Reinsurance Undertakings (Prudential Requirements) Regulations 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assets and liabilities are valued in accordance with rules made by the Prudential Regulation Authority under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 in relation to the matching adjustment referred to in subsection (5)(e)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assets and liabilities are valued in accordance with other rules made by the Authority under that Part implementing Articles 75 to 85 and 308b to 308e of the Solvency 2 Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assets and liabilities are valued in accordance with Articles 7 to 52 and 55 to 61 of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2015/35` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833A(7) the company's assets and liabilities are valued as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `the assets and liabilities are valued in accordance with Part 2 of the Insurance and Reinsurance Undertakings (Prudential Requirements) Regulations 2023`
       AND `the assets and liabilities are valued in accordance with rules made by the Prudential Regulation Authority under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 in relation to the matching adjustment referred to in subsection (5)(e)(i)`
       AND `the assets and liabilities are valued in accordance with other rules made by the Authority under that Part implementing Articles 75 to 85 and 308b to 308e of the Solvency 2 Directive`
       AND `the assets and liabilities are valued in accordance with Articles 7 to 52 and 55 to 61 of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2015/35`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company’s assets and liabilities must be valued in accordance with— (a) Part 2 of the Insurance and Reinsurance Undertakings (Prudential Requirements) Regulations 2023 ..., (b) rules made by the Prudential Regulation Authority ..., (c) other rules made by the Authority ..., and (d) Articles 7 to 52 and 55 to 61 of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2015/35"

-- src:11221 | (8) If the company carries on both long-term business and other insurance business—
-- src:11222 | (a) this section is to be applied on the assumption that the company carries on only the long-term business; and
-- src:11223 | (b) the remainder of this Part is to be applied on the assumption that the company carries on only that other insurance business;
-- src:11224 | and, in applying paragraph (a) or (b), such apportionments of amounts referable to the long-term business or other insurance business are to be made as are just and reasonable.
@ref s 833A(8) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11221-11224)
GIVEN `the company carries on both long-term business and other insurance business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833A(8)(a) this section is applied on the assumption that the company carries on only the long-term business` MEANS
    IF `the company carries on both long-term business and other insurance business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company carries on both long-term business and other insurance business— (a) this section is to be applied on the assumption that the company carries on only the long-term business"

@ref s 833A(8)(b) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11223-11223)
GIVEN `the company carries on both long-term business and other insurance business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833A(8)(b) the remainder of this Part is applied on the assumption that the company carries on only that other insurance business` MEANS
    IF `the company carries on both long-term business and other insurance business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company carries on both long-term business and other insurance business— ... (b) the remainder of this Part is to be applied on the assumption that the company carries on only that other insurance business"

@ref s 833A(8) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11224-11224)
GIVEN `the amount referable to the long-term business or other insurance business that the company's records show` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of that amount that is just and reasonable to apportion to the business concerned` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 833A(8) the amount apportioned to the business concerned` MEANS
    `the amount referable to the long-term business or other insurance business that the company's records show` TIMES `the proportion of that amount that is just and reasonable to apportion to the business concerned`

-- src:11225 | (9) In this section—
-- src:11226 | “best estimate”, “paid-in ordinary share capital”, “paid-in preference shares”, “relevant risk-free interest rate term structure” and “ring-fenced fund” have the same meaning as in rules made by the Prudential Regulation Authority under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, as they have effect from time to time;
-- src:11227 | “defined benefit pension scheme” means a pension scheme (as defined by section 1(5) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993) which is a defined benefits scheme within the meaning given by section 2 of the Pension Schemes Act 2015;
-- src:11228 | “long-term business” means business that consists of effecting or carrying out contracts of long-term insurance (and this definition must be read with section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, any relevant order under that section and Schedule 2 to that Act);
-- src:11229 | “qualifying investment subsidiary” means an undertaking in which the company holds a participation within the meaning given by Article 13(20) of the Solvency 2 Directive and which is not held by the company as part of its portfolio of investments;
-- src:11230 | “Solvency 2 Directive” means Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council on the taking-up and pursuit of the business of Insurance and Reinsurance (Solvency II).
@ref s 833A(9) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11225-11230)
GIVEN `the term has the same meaning as in rules made by the Prudential Regulation Authority under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, as they have effect from time to time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833A(9) the term has the meaning given by the Prudential Regulation Authority's rules` MEANS
    `the term has the same meaning as in rules made by the Prudential Regulation Authority under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, as they have effect from time to time` -- JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE is the borrowed definition's answer, supplied by the caller; NOTHING (points outside the text) stays NOTHING

@ref s 833A(9) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11227-11227)
GIVEN `the scheme is a pension scheme as defined by section 1(5) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme is a defined benefits scheme within the meaning given by section 2 of the Pension Schemes Act 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833A(9) the scheme is a defined benefit pension scheme` MEANS
    IF `the scheme is a pension scheme as defined by section 1(5) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993` AND `the scheme is a defined benefits scheme within the meaning given by section 2 of the Pension Schemes Act 2015`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“defined benefit pension scheme” means a pension scheme (as defined by section 1(5) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993) which is a defined benefits scheme within the meaning given by section 2 of the Pension Schemes Act 2015"

@ref s 833A(9) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11228-11228)
GIVEN `the business consists of effecting or carrying out contracts of long-term insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833A(9) the business is long-term business` MEANS
    IF `the business consists of effecting or carrying out contracts of long-term insurance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“long-term business” means business that consists of effecting or carrying out contracts of long-term insurance" (read with s 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, outside the sources)

@ref s 833A(9) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11229-11229)
GIVEN `the undertaking is one in which the company holds a participation within the meaning given by Article 13(20) of the Solvency 2 Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the participation is held by the company as part of its portfolio of investments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833A(9) the undertaking is a qualifying investment subsidiary` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is one in which the company holds a participation within the meaning given by Article 13(20) of the Solvency 2 Directive` AND (NOT `the participation is held by the company as part of its portfolio of investments`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualifying investment subsidiary” means an undertaking in which the company holds a participation within the meaning given by Article 13(20) of the Solvency 2 Directive and which is not held by the company as part of its portfolio of investments"

@ref s 833A(9) Distributions by insurance companies authorised under the Solvency 2 Directive (src:11230-11230)
GIVEN `the instrument is Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council on the taking-up and pursuit of the business of Insurance and Reinsurance (Solvency II)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 833A(9) the instrument is the Solvency 2 Directive` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council on the taking-up and pursuit of the business of Insurance and Reinsurance (Solvency II)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Solvency 2 Directive” means Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council on the taking-up and pursuit of the business of Insurance and Reinsurance (Solvency II)."

-- ss 834 and 835 are shown as dots in the text (repealed or blank): see the coverage table in NOTES.md.
